{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"The first thing I would have to tell you for a good morning, namely that we arrived here safely, partly follows from this itself; the company were decent people; it got cold at night; yet four woolen body linings or skirts protected me sufficiently, so that I, after having with difficulty peeled myself off again, have remained unharmed. Yesterday at noon at 1 o'clock we arrived here, but it is harder to get out of Magdeburg than to come in. — The activity of Mr. Post President and the Prussian intelligence have not yet cast their eye on the local post coach business, at least insofar as it concerns my interest. Until Tuesday noon only does the — I almost said — coach to Cassel go. The journaliers with which I came is not connected with any further courses. To stay here until Tuesday is far too long. So I resolved first, since tomorrow morning the traveling coach to Erfurt goes, to take my course thither; how nice, to bring Goethe the package, which I would have to send from here, myself and from there to go on along the great highway! — Thereupon I looked at the post coach, but what a cart! and then I would have to drive about 44 miles to Cassel — so I decided to take extra post, but I have to hear that I would be carried on further on the same cart, wagon, under open sky. With this briefly resolved, to return quickly to Berlin and to fetch my traveling coach, and with this well equipped, to pleasantly continue my health journey. With this cheerful thought, to see you dear ones again soon, I then fell asleep and slept very well; yet, you see, not, like Peter, in the sense of staying at home, but on the contrary to travel out thoroughly. The former would otherwise have been no wonder either, for I indeed went on the journey with greater reluctance than I dared to say, and if I had not already received the money, it would have been hard to bring me to it, so necessary it was to me in fact. Besides, I also yesterday afternoon saw what there was to see here; — the famous cathedral — it may be remarkable, because it is a cathedral; — but the whole architecture is not such a good conception as the Nuremberg Gothic churches, and what of artwork is inside, a lot of carved and cast, painted and plastered, is far too bad. The cast apostles by Fischer, the Nuremberger, are not to be compared with the Nurembergers. The subjects have entirely fallen into the craft! The dearest thing I have seen is General Carnot, a lovable old man and Frenchman; it is the famous one; — he took it friendly that I visited him. — Then I strolled on the Elbe, a fleet of 13 Hamburg ships with high-swollen sea sails was coming in (each with two, yet only on one mast), beautiful stream, beautiful immeasurable fertile plains (here fertile, but otherwise between Potsdam and Burg, what we saw by day, quite desolate) — more beautiful the clearest sky. Just now a coachman comes, who has to bring an Englishman, who seems to be a German, to Cassel in 3 days; to him I will attach myself..."}}],"created":1795218912,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":688,"prompt_tokens":882,"total_tokens":1570,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-3B5MeUWAitjnraYUKysNQsNNEi9NaeiW","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":882,"prompt_ms":888.542,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0074172335600908,"prompt_per_second":992.6373767362712,"predicted_n":688,"predicted_ms":16375.312,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.835970887918485,"predicted_per_second":41.95339911691454}}